.TH INTRO 8 "September 27, 2026"
.UC 2
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to system maintenance and operation commands
.SH DESCRIPTION
This section contains information related to system operation
and maintenance.
It describes commands used to create new file systems,
.BR newfs ,
verify the integrity of the file systems,
.BR fsck ,
control disk usage,
.BR edquota ,
maintain system backups,
.BR dump ,
.BR rdump ,
recover files when disks die an untimely death,
.BR restore ,
add user accounts,
.BR adduser ,
detect devices for the kernel,
.BR autoconfig ,
boot the kernel and start system services,
.BR boot ,
.BR rc ,
file bug reports,
.BR bugfiler ,
guidlines for analyzing kernel crashes,
.BR crash ,
enable/disable terminal lines,
.BR getty ,
manage the printing subsystem,
.BR lpc ,
.BR lpd ,
.BR pac ,
create the device name to major/minor database,
.BR makedev ,
generate encryption keys,
.BR makekey ,
send/receive mail,
.BR sendmail ,
persistent text and append-only directories,
.BR sticky ,
synchronize buffer cache to disk,
.BR sync ,
maintain system time,
.BR timed ,
.BR timedc,
the uucp communications system,
.BR uucico ,
.BR uuclean ,
.BR uupoll ,
.BR uusnap ,
.B uuxqt
